|~ Every value comes apart into the set of its atoms and a shape, and
   the shape applied to the set builds the value back [D42], [D82]. The
   atoms are the values no verb takes further apart, null, booleans,
   numbers, strings, keywords and tag names, each once, in the one
   order, and a value is taken apart to the end: the keys of its maps
   and the tags over its payloads are atoms as its other leaves are.
   The shape is a quote of projections into the set and of the steps
   that build the value from what they read: a vector is the vector of
   the shapes of its elements; a map is built from the pairs of its keys
   and values by `indexBy`; a tagged value, the set and the quote among
   them, from its tag and its payload by `tag`; an error from its
   descriptor by `error`; and a doc from its text by `parse`.
   `["x" [1 1] {:b :a}]` has the atoms `#[1 "x" :a :b]` and the shape
   `~([/1 [/0 /0] ([[/3 /2]] | indexBy ~(first) * last)])`. The verbs
   are the language's own, and the test of the ring runs them over every
   example of the catalog and every literal of the conformance cases. ~|

:atomKinds
  |~~ The kinds of the atoms. ~~|
  #[::null ::boolean ::number ::string ::keyword ::tag]

:asPairs
  |~~ Each element of a vector as the pair of whether it failed and the
      value its parts are taken from: an error as the descriptor the
      fail track reads, any other value as it is. The error rides a
      second error past the step that pairs a value, which leaves its
      trail on the second. ~~|
  ::verb~(* (!| error {:failed /} | [false /] !| [true /failed]))

:groupBefore
  |~~ The step followed by the steps of the suffix, as a group, or the
      step alone under an empty suffix. ~~|
  ::verb~(
    :suffix ::vec
    | if (suffix | count | eq 0) ~() ~([[/] suffix] | flat | tag ::quote | tag ::group))

:partsOf
  |~~ The parts a value that is no atom is built from, and the steps
      that build it from them: a vector from its elements by none, a map
      from the pairs of its keys and values, a doc from its text, and a
      tagged value from its tag and its payload, an error from its
      descriptor among them. ~~|
  ::verb~(
    :failed ::boolean
    | :kind (type)
    | cond
        ~(kind | eq ::vec) ~({:parts / :glue ~()})
        ~(kind | eq ::map) ~(:entries / | {:parts (keys | sort * (:key / | [key (entries | at key)])) :glue ~(indexBy ~(first) * last)})
        ~(kind | eq ::doc) ~({:parts [(json | parseJson)] :glue ~(first | parse | first)})
        ~({:parts [kind (payload)] :glue (if failed ~(~(tag | error)) ~(~(tag)))}))

:intoAtoms
  |~~ The atoms gathered so far with those of one pair after them.
      `reduce` folds it over the pairs of a vector, and it folds itself
      over the parts of each value it meets. ~~|
  ::verb~(
    :pair ::vec
    | :gathered /
    | pair | /1
    | if (atomKinds | has (pair | /1 | type))
        ~(gathered | append (pair | /1))
        ~(partsOf (pair | /0) | /parts | asPairs | reduce gathered ~(intoAtoms)))

:numberedWith
  |~~ The atoms numbered so far, `{:next … :pairs …}`, with one more. ~~|
  ::verb~(
    :atom ::any
    | :acc /
    | {:next (acc | /next | add 1) :pairs (acc | /pairs | append [atom (acc | /next)])})

:intoShape
  |~~ The steps built so far, `{:numbered … :steps …}`, with the step of
      one pair after them: the projection of an atom's place in the set,
      which the pairs of `:numbered` hold, or the step that builds a
      value from the steps of its parts. ~~|
  ::verb~(
    :pair ::vec
    | :acc /
    | pair | /1
    | if (atomKinds | has (pair | /1 | type))
        ~(:atom /
          | {:numbered (acc | /numbered)
             :steps (acc | /steps | append ({:path [(acc | /numbered | filter ~(first | eq atom) | first | last)]} | tag ::proj))})
        ~(partsOf (pair | /0) | :built /
          | built | /parts | asPairs | reduce {:numbered (acc | /numbered) :steps []} ~(intoShape) | :inner /
          | {:numbered (acc | /numbered) :steps (acc | /steps | append (inner | /steps | groupBefore (built | /glue)))}))

:apart
  |~~ The atoms of the subject and its shape.

      ~(["x" [1 1] {:b :a}] | apart | eq {:atoms #[1 "x" :a :b] :shape ~([/1 [/0 /0] ([[/3 /2]] | indexBy ~(first) * last)])})
  ~~|
  ::verb~(
    :held [/]
    | :atoms (held | asPairs | reduce [] ~(intoAtoms) | tag ::set)
    | :numbered (atoms | reduce {:next 0 :pairs []} ~(numberedWith) | /pairs)
    | {:atoms atoms :shape (held | asPairs | reduce {:numbered numbered :steps []} ~(intoShape) | /steps | tag ::quote)})

:rebuilt
  |~~ The value the shape of the subject builds from its atoms. ~~|
  ::verb~(apart | :pieces / | pieces | /atoms | apply (pieces | /shape))

:survives
  |~~ Whether the value its pieces build is the subject. A value that is
      an error goes in a vector, since it deflects around a verb. ~~|
  ::verb~(:original / | rebuilt | eq original)
